gl5: the integrand was evaluated before the n_points guard

The discriminating control for `gauss_legendre_5_guard_precedes_f_neg`, which
asserts that the guard is reached before this integrand. That claim is only
worth something if the integrand is reachable at all: a `gauss_legendre_5`
that never applied `f`, or an elided call, would satisfy the ordering
expectation for the wrong reason. Same integrand, same interval, `n_points`
changed from 20 to the one supported order, and the trap that fires is the
integrand's. The message names the ordering because it is the same def; here
it means the opposite, which is the point.
